  "id": "COMPOUND:23441 - PROTEIN:5798",
  "verbalization": "Corticatic Acid E is implicated in the interaction with NH-6 through a multi-step pathway involving a dual serine/threonine and tyrosine protein kinase. This kinase is targeted by 6-Acetonyldihydrochelerythrine and also by CID 21778290, which in turn targets NH-6. The evidence suggests that Corticatic Acid E may act as a modulator of the downstream signaling cascade initiated by these kinases, potentially influencing the activity of NH-6 through a complex network of interactions. The presence of multiple targets and their shared involvement in the same pathway highlights a possible mechanism where Corticatic Acid E could regulate the expression or function of the downstream kinases, thereby affecting NH-6. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of the kinase pathway in mediating the effects of Corticatic Acid E on NH-6, suggesting a role in cellular signaling or metabolic regulation.",
